IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- SCHEDULE 7 -- CONSEQUENTIAL AMENDMENTS (S.I. 2017/692, lines 3544-3794 of the plain-text rendering, which is not the official text and is
-- not verified against it).
--
-- WHAT IT IS.  Thirty-five paragraphs that amend other Acts and other instruments so that they fit these Regulations: "for the Money Laundering
-- Regulations 2007 substitute ...", "omit paragraph ...", "after subsection (7) insert ...".  The brief's reason 2 puts amendments of other Acts
-- outside the encoding as machinery, and nearly all of this Schedule is that: an instruction to change words in a text that is not among the sources
-- cannot be applied, and the changed text is not a rule of these Regulations.
--
-- WHAT IS ENCODED.  Three paragraphs INSERT whole rules whose wording stands alone, and each says something to a person or a business:
--   * paragraph 3(2): section 226(7A) to (7D) of FSMA, the ombudsman rules must make a person wrongly identified as a politically exposed person
--     (or a family member or close associate) eligible to complain (lines 3555-3564);
--   * paragraph 12: paragraph 2A of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991, the duty to forward details of an
--     offer does not apply to an estate agent that cannot complete customer due diligence (lines 3682-3686);
--   * paragraph 18: regulation 48(2) and (3) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001, a company authorised on or after the day
--     these Regulations came into force may not issue bearer shares, subject to an exception (lines 3703-3711).
-- Paragraph 18's first limb ("may not issue any bearer shares") names its bearer, the company, so the prohibition is also written as a rule with SHANT, derived from the no (ruling N2).
-- Each encodes the inserted words only.  The host provision they sit in (section 226 of FSMA, paragraph 2 of the Order, regulation 48(1) of the
-- 2001 Regulations) is not among the sources, so a case outside the inserted words answers NOTHING ("points outside the text").  Everything else in
-- the Schedule is inert, reason 2 (NOTES.md, Coverage).
--
-- THE REGULATIONS' OWN DATE.  "The day on which these Regulations came into force" (paragraph 18(b)) is the core's constant
-- `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force`, 26 June 2017.

-- src:3544 | SCHEDULE 7 — Consequential Amendments
§ `Schedule 7 -- Consequential Amendments`

DECLARE `sch 7 para 3(2) defined term` IS ONE OF
    `sch 7 para 3(2) politically exposed person`
    `sch 7 para 3(2) family member`
    `sch 7 para 3(2) known close associate`

-- The party and the act of the prohibition in paragraph 18(c), regulation 48(2) (ruling N2: where the text names who bears a prohibition, the prohibition is derived from the no).
DECLARE `sch 7 party` IS ONE OF
    `sch 7 an open-ended investment company authorised on or after the relevant date`

DECLARE `sch 7 act` IS ONE OF
    `sch 7 issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)`

-- src:3555 | (2) In section 226 (complaints: the ombudsman scheme etc) after subsection (7) insert—
-- src:3556 | (7A) The rules must provide that a person within subsection (7B) is eligible in relation to a complaint to which subsection (7C) applies.
-- src:3557 | (7B) A person is within this subsection if he or she has been identified by a respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as—
-- src:3558 | (a) a politically exposed person;
-- src:3559 | (b) a family member of a politically exposed person; or
-- src:3560 | (c) a known close associate of a politically exposed person.
-- src:3561 | (7C) This subsection applies to a complaint—
-- src:3562 | (a) that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B); or
-- src:3563 | (b) relating to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B).
-- src:3564 | (7D) In subsection (7B), “politically exposed person”, “family member” and “known close associate” have the meanings given in regulation 35(12) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.
-- Section 226(7B): who is within the subsection.  "A person is within this subsection if" is a condition the text introduces with "if": a person
-- who has not been so identified is outside it.
@ref sch 7 para 3(2) (src:3555-3564)
GIVEN `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7B) the person is within the subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` OR `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` OR `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is within this subsection if he or she has been identified by a respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as— (a) a politically exposed person; (b) a family member of a politically exposed person; or (c) a known close associate of a politically exposed person." (marginal reading (a))

-- Section 226(7C): the complaints it applies to.  The text lists two kinds and does not close the list with "only".
@ref sch 7 para 3(2) (src:3561-3563)
GIVEN `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7C) the complaint is one to which the subsection applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` OR `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This subsection applies to a complaint— (a) ...; or (b) ..." names two kinds of complaint and does not say that no other complaint is within it

-- Section 226(7A): "The rules must provide that a person within subsection (7B) is eligible in relation to a complaint to which subsection (7C) applies."
-- The text does not say whose rules (the host section does): no actor is named here, so no regulative rule is written (FORK S7-F2).
@ref sch 7 para 3(2) (src:3556)
GIVEN `the person is within subsection (7B)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the complaint is one to which subsection (7C) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7A) the rules must provide that the person is eligible in relation to the complaint` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is within subsection (7B)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the complaint is one to which subsection (7C) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names a person within (7B) and a complaint to which (7C) applies; whether anyone else is eligible is for the rest of section 226, which is not among the sources

-- Section 226(7D): the three terms have the meanings given in regulation 35(12) of these Regulations (encoded by part mlr2).  A pointer.
@ref sch 7 para 3(2) (src:3564)
GIVEN term IS A `sch 7 para 3(2) defined term`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7D) the term has the meaning given in` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `sch 7 para 3(2) politically exposed person` THEN "regulation 35(12)"
    WHEN `sch 7 para 3(2) family member` THEN "regulation 35(12)"
    WHEN `sch 7 para 3(2) known close associate` THEN "regulation 35(12)"

-- src:3682 | 12 Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991
-- src:3683 | Schedule 3 (other matters) to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991 is amended as follows—
-- src:3684 | (a) at the beginning of paragraph 2, insert “ Subject to paragraph 2A ”;
-- src:3685 | (b) after paragraph 2, insert—
-- src:3686 | Paragraph 2 does not apply if the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer because the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28, and where relevant, those required by regulations 33, and 35 to 37 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 in relation to the offeror.
-- Paragraph 2A of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991.  "Paragraph 2 does not apply if ..." is a flat negative
-- with a condition.  Paragraph 2 itself (the duty to forward offers) is in the Order and is not among the sources.
-- "unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28, and where relevant, those required by regulations 33, and 35 to 37":
-- read as unable to apply the measures that are required, which is unable to apply those of regulation 28 or, where relevant, those of the others
-- (FORK S7-F1; the other reading needs inability on both).
@ref sch 7 para 12 (src:3682-3686)
GIVEN `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 12 paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991 applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer`
           AND (`the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` OR (`regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` AND `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph 2 does not apply if the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer because the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28, and where relevant, those required by regulations 33, and 35 to 37 ..."
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Order is not among the sources, so whether it applies in any other case is not answered

-- src:3703 | 18 Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001
-- src:3704 | Regulation 48 (bearer shares) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 is amended as follows—
-- src:3705 | (a) the existing text is renumbered as paragraph (1);
-- src:3706 | (b) in that paragraph (1), after “investment company” insert “ authorised before the day on which the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 came into force (“the relevant date”) ”;
-- src:3707 | (c) after paragraph (1) insert—
-- src:3708 | (2) An open-ended investment company authorised on or after the relevant date may not issue any bearer shares under paragraph (1), and any provision in the instrument of incorporation of such an open-ended investment company purporting to authorise it to do so is void.
-- src:3709 | (3) Paragraph (2) does not apply to an open-ended investment company if—
-- src:3710 | (a) an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to that open-ended investment company before the relevant date; and
-- src:3711 | (b) that application was not determined until a date on or after the relevant date.
-- Regulation 48 of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001, as amended.  Limb (b) inserts "authorised before the day on which [these
-- Regulations] came into force ('the relevant date')" into paragraph (1): the relevant date is the core's constant.
@ref sch 7 para 18 (src:3703-3711)
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 7 para 18(b) the relevant date` MEANS `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force`

-- Paragraph (3): the exception to paragraph (2).  "Paragraph (2) does not apply to an open-ended investment company if" the application for an
-- authorisation order was made before the relevant date and not determined until on or after it.
@ref sch 7 para 18 (src:3709-3711)
GIVEN `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date on which that application was determined` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (3) the application was made before and determined on or after the relevant date` MEANS
        `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` LESS THAN `sch 7 para 18(b) the relevant date`
    AND `the date on which that application was determined` AT LEAST `sch 7 para 18(b) the relevant date`

-- Paragraph (2): "An open-ended investment company authorised on or after the relevant date may not issue any bearer shares under paragraph (1)".
-- A flat negative, so the text's no; it is lifted by paragraph (3).  Whether a company authorised before the relevant date may is paragraph (1),
-- which is not among the sources.
@ref sch 7 para 18 (src:3708)
GIVEN `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS A DATE
      `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date on which that application was determined` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the open-ended investment company may issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` AT LEAST `sch 7 para 18(b) the relevant date`
           AND (NOT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (3) the application was made before and determined on or after the relevant date` `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` `the date on which that application was determined`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An open-ended investment company authorised on or after the relevant date may not issue any bearer shares under paragraph (1)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraph (1) of regulation 48 is not among the sources, and paragraph (3) lifts paragraph (2) without saying what then follows

-- The prohibition derived from the answer above (ruling N2): the company is the party the text names; no time limit, remedy or other consequence is stated, so there is no WITHIN and no LEST.
@ref sch 7 para 18 (src:3708)
GIVEN `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS A DATE
      `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date on which that application was determined` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 7 party` `sch 7 act`
`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the prohibition on issuing bearer shares` MEANS
    IF (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the open-ended investment company may issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)` `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` `the date on which that application was determined`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY `sch 7 an open-ended investment company authorised on or after the relevant date`
         SHANT `sch 7 issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Paragraph (2), second limb: "any provision in the instrument of incorporation of such an open-ended investment company purporting to authorise it to do so is void."
@ref sch 7 para 18 (src:3708)
GIVEN `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS A DATE
      `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date on which that application was determined` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the provision in the instrument of incorporation is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares`
           AND `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` AT LEAST `sch 7 para 18(b) the relevant date`
           AND (NOT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (3) the application was made before and determined on or after the relevant date` `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` `the date on which that application was determined`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares`
           AND `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` LESS THAN `sch 7 para 18(b) the relevant date`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "authorised on or after the relevant date" is a date the text fixes in its own words, read like a period, so a company authorised before it is outside paragraph (2) and its provision is not voided by it (assumed, not ruled: FORK S7-F2)
        IF     `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares`
           AND `sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (3) the application was made before and determined on or after the relevant date` `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` `the date on which that application was determined`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) does not apply to an open-ended investment company if— (a) an application for an authorisation order was made ... before the relevant date; and (b) that application was not determined until a date on or after the relevant date"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph voids a provision in the instrument "purporting to authorise" the issue of bearer shares, and says nothing where there is no such provision

